{"uid":"13038b4147280736","name":"A deleted contact leaves no row behind","fullName":"tests.db_tests.test_storage_facts#test_a_deleted_contact_leaves_no_row_behind","historyId":"8c4d2722996180eab5d70a69c061b4aa","time":{"start":1787223759770,"stop":1787223759791,"duration":21},"description":"The API cannot see this: `404` looks identical whether the row is gone or\nmerely hidden behind a filter.\n\nThis is not a guard against a hypothetical refactor. It encodes a\ndata-retention decision this system has made: **deletion here is physical,\nand personal data does not survive it.** A contact carries an email address\nand a name; when someone asks for that to be removed, \"removed\" has to mean\nthe row is gone, not that a flag now excludes it from queries.\n\nIf that decision ever changes — a `deleted_at` column, an archive table, a\ntombstone — this test fails, and it should. The conversation it forces is the\npoint of it. Every HTTP test would keep passing through such a change while\nthe data quietly stayed.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>The API cannot see this: <code>404</code> looks identical whether the row is gone or<br />\nmerely hidden behind a filter.</p>\n<p>This is not a guard against a hypothetical refactor. It encodes a<br />\ndata-retention decision this system has made: <strong>deletion here is physical,<br />\nand personal data does not survive it.</strong> A contact carries an email address<br />\nand a name; when someone asks for that to be removed, &quot;removed&quot; has to mean<br />\nthe row is gone, not that a flag now excludes it from queries.</p>\n<p>If that decision ever changes — a <code>deleted_at</code> column, an archive table, a<br />\ntombstone — this test fails, and it should. The conversation it forces is the<br />\npoint of it. Every HTTP test would keep passing through such a change while<br />\nthe data quietly stayed.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesS